## Layout

{% if cookiecutter.crate_type != 'lib' -%}
- `scripts/` holds the toolchain helpers and the bundler (`bundle.py`, `smoke_bundle.py`), with
  their tests beside them as `scripts/test_<script>.py`.
{%- else -%}
- `scripts/` holds the toolchain helpers, with their tests beside them as
  `scripts/test_<script>.py`.
{%- endif %}
- Do not add first-party `.py` files for Rust to run. `[project.dependencies]` is what the
  embedded interpreter imports, through `import_fn` in `crates/py`; see `write-code`.
- pytest collects `scripts/` with `--doctest-modules`, so every module there is imported at
  collection and every docstring example runs.
